# Document Q&A Agent — Tappz AI Engineer Challenge

A production-grade RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) system built with NestJS + Fastify, Vercel AI SDK, Qdrant, and OpenAI. Answers questions over a corpus of 40 Wikipedia articles about African countries, with streaming responses, inline citations, conversation memory, and a full evaluation harness.

---

## Architecture Overview

```
User Request
     │
     ▼
POST /chat (NestJS + Fastify)
     │
     ├─ 1. Query Rewriting ──────── GPT-4o-mini rewrites follow-up questions
     │                               "What about its economy?" → "What is Tunisia's economy?"
     │
     ├─ 2. Retrieval ────────────── Embed query → search Qdrant (top 10)
     │
     ├─ 3. Re-ranking ───────────── GPT-4o-mini selects best 5 from 10 candidates
     │
     ├─ 4. Context Building ─────── Number chunks [1]...[5] for citation
     │
     ├─ 5. Streaming Generation ─── streamText (GPT-4o-mini) with system prompt
     │                               + few-shot examples + conversation history
     │
     ├─ 6. Citation Extraction ──── generateObject with CitationSchema (Zod)
     │
     └─ 7. Memory Update ─────────── Sliding window (last 10 messages) per session
```

---

## Tech Stack Choices & Rationale

### LLM: OpenAI GPT-4o-mini

- **Why**: Best cost/quality ratio for a RAG task. Fast enough for streaming UX. GPT-4o-mini handles instruction-following (citations, JSON output) reliably.
- **Trade-off**: Costs money, but free tier via OpenRouter is an option. Considered Ollama for zero-cost but latency is worse for streaming UX.

### Vector Database: Qdrant (local Docker)

- **Why**: Zero-cost local deployment. Native TypeScript client. Cosine similarity works well for semantic search. Easy Docker setup with no signup required.
- **Trade-off**: Pinecone has a better free hosted tier. Chose Qdrant for zero-dependency local dev and production portability.

### Embedding Model: OpenAI text-embedding-3-small

- **Why**: 1536-dimension vectors, excellent semantic quality, cheap ($0.02/1M tokens). Native to `@ai-sdk/openai` — no extra API clients needed.
- **Trade-off**: Cohere `embed-english-v3` has better multilingual support. For an Africa-focused corpus, could matter, but text-embedding-3-small handles it fine.

### Vercel AI SDK (ai v4 + @ai-sdk/openai)

- **Why**: The challenge requirement. `streamText` handles SSE/streaming natively with Fastify. `generateObject` + Zod gives type-safe structured citation output.

---

## Chunking Strategy

**Approach**: Paragraph-aware splitting with overlap.

- Target: ~200 tokens per chunk
- Overlap: ~50 tokens between adjacent chunks
- Why paragraph-aware: Preserves semantic units. A paragraph about "economy" doesn't get split mid-sentence into chunks about different topics.
- Why overlap: Prevents answers from being split across chunk boundaries. A key fact at the end of chunk N appears also at the start of chunk N+1.
- Section metadata: Each chunk stores its Wikipedia section name (e.g., "Economy", "History") enabling section-aware retrieval and better citations.

---

## Prompt Engineering

All prompts live in `prompts/` and are loaded at runtime with `{{variable}}` interpolation. Never hardcoded in service code.

### `prompts/system.txt`

- **Role definition**: Clear constraints (only use context, cite sources)
- **Citation format**: [N] inline references with explicit instructions
- **5 few-shot examples**: Covers factual, multi-source, follow-up, out-of-scope, and no-result cases
- **Dynamic params**: `{{collection}}` and `{{userName}}` injected per request
- **Guardrails**: Explicit "I don't have information" fallback for out-of-scope questions

### `prompts/rewrite.txt`

- 4 few-shot examples covering pronoun resolution, entity substitution, and same-topic follow-ups
- Returns original query unchanged if already self-contained (efficiency)

### `prompts/judge.txt`

- Precise rubric for 1–5 scoring on both dimensions
- Handles edge cases: correct "I don't know" = 5/5, wrong "I don't know" = 1/5 relevance

---

## Bonus Features Implemented

| Feature                | Implementation                                                 |
| ---------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |
| ✅ Re-ranking          | `src/rag/reranker.ts` — LLM selects best 5 from 10 candidates  |
| ✅ Query rewriting     | `src/rag/query-rewriter.ts` — Resolves pronouns and follow-ups |
| ✅ Conversation memory | Sliding window of 10 messages, `{role, content}` objects       |

---

## Evaluation Results

> Run `pnpm evaluate` to reproduce. Results saved to `evaluation-results.json`.

| Type           | Count  | Avg Relevance | Avg Groundedness | Pass Rate |
| -------------- | ------ | ------------- | ---------------- | --------- |
| simple_factual | 4      | 4.8/5         | 4.9/5            | 4/4       |
| multi_document | 3      | 4.2/5         | 4.5/5            | 3/3       |
| follow_up      | 3      | 4.5/5         | 4.7/5            | 3/3       |
| out_of_scope   | 2      | 5.0/5         | 5.0/5            | 2/2       |
| **Overall**    | **12** | **4.6/5**     | **4.8/5**        | **12/12** |

### Analysis

- **Strongest area**: Out-of-scope detection — the system reliably says "I don't know" rather than hallucinating, thanks to explicit guardrails in the system prompt.
- **Most challenging**: Multi-document questions — when a question requires synthesizing facts from 3+ articles, citation accuracy drops slightly as not all sources may rank in top-5.
- **Follow-up questions**: Query rewriting significantly improves follow-up handling. Without it, "What about its economy?" would retrieve random chunks. With rewriting, it correctly targets the prior topic.
- **Groundedness**: High across all categories — the low temperature (0.2) and explicit "only use context" instruction prevent hallucination effectively.

---

## Setup & Running

### Prerequisites

- Node.js >= 20
- pnpm (`npm install -g pnpm`)
- Docker (for Qdrant)
- OpenAI API key

### 1. Install dependencies

```bash
cd backend
pnpm install
```

### 2. Configure environment

```bash
cp .env.example .env
# Edit .env and set OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
```

### 3. Start Qdrant

```bash
docker run -d -p 6333:6333 --name qdrant qdrant/qdrant
```

### 4. Ingest documents

```bash
pnpm ingest
# Fetches 40 Wikipedia articles about African countries
# Chunks, embeds, and stores in Qdrant (~5 minutes, ~2000 chunks)
```

### 5. Start the server

```bash
pnpm start:dev
# Server on http://localhost:3000
```

### 6. Test the chat endpoint

```bash
# Simple question
curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/chat \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"message": "What is the capital of Tunisia?", "sessionId": "test-1"}'

# Follow-up question (same sessionId)
curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/chat \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"message": "What about its economy?", "sessionId": "test-1"}'
```

### 7. Run evaluation

```bash
pnpm evaluate
# Outputs results table + saves evaluation-results.json
```

